   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Explanation \n",
    "#### .loc[]\n",
    "- It is label-based indexing. It is used to access a group of rows and columns in a DataFrame by their labels (names) --- not by their integer positions.\n",
    "- syntax : ```df.loc[row_condition, column_label]```\n",
    "  - row_condition: A condition or label(s) that tells pandas which rows you want.\n",
    "  - column_label: The column(s) you want from those selected rows."
   ]
  },
