  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ac5a3a1c-48a3-4485-add5-7e6549dc2b54",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Here thresh i.e threshold means the minimum amount of data that a row must have for it to be allowed to be white listed when .dropna() method is ran in pandas. \n",
    "- Basically It's saying that :\n",
    "  - If there are 11 columns in the dataFrame\n",
    "  - If there is a row where out of 11 columns 10 of them have values in it and 1 of them has a NaN value in it.\n",
    "  - If ```df.dropna(thresh=10)``` where ```thresh=10``` then what it means is that all the rows that have 1 column with ```NaN``` value and 10 columns with data then It will not be dropped by ```.dropna()``` method. It will be allowed to be remained in the dataFrame after processing\n",
    "  - All the other rows that do not fit in this rule defined in ```thresh``` will be dropped."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5b7a103c-9384-4f68-944f-746ce981ba93",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Insert the missing date in the dataFrame where the date column is set to be the index of the dataFrame\n",
    "Refer to this docs for more info : https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.date_range.html"
   ]
  },
